        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): propagate parent abort signal to spawned ACP child sessions",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a parent session is cancelled (user presses Stop, session timeout), child ACP sessions spawned via `sessions_spawn(runtime=\"acp\")` continue running because the cancellation signal was never linked to the child runtime handle. The child subprocess becomes orphaned, consuming CPU and memory until its own timeout.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`spawnAcpDirect` initializes a child ACP runtime handle (`runtimeCloseHandle`) but never links it to the parent session lifecycle. The `execute` handler in `sessions_spawn` already receives an `AbortSignal` from the agent execution framework — it was simply not forwarded.\n\nThe fix registers an abort listener that calls `cleanupFailedAcpSpawn` (runtime.close + session deletion) when the parent signal fires.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents orphaned ACP child processes when parent sessions are cancelled\n- Reduces CPU/memory waste on constrained hosts\n- No change to normal ACP spawn behavior (only activates on abort)\n\n## Evidence — Real Behavior Proof\n\n```\n$ npx tsx proof/acp-abort-propagation.proof.ts\n\n─── 1. SpawnAcpContext type includes abortSignal ───\n  ✅ Type field abortSignal?: AbortSignal present: true\n  ✅ Abort signal read from ctx: true\n  ✅ Abort listener registered: true\n  ✅ Pre-abort check (signal already aborted): true\n\n─── 2. Signal forwarded from sessions_spawn tool execute handler ───\n  ✅ Execute handler receives signal param: true\n  ✅ Signal forwarded to SpawnAcpContext: true\n\n─── 3. Unit tests: 66 passed ───\n\n─── 4. Code review: no behavioral regressions ───\n  ✅ Abort listener guarded: only when session+handle exist\n  ✅ Listener code is after catch block (normal flow unaffected)\n```\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/acp-spawn.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  66 passed (66)\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- `src/agents/acp-spawn.ts`: +33 lines (abortSignal type field + abort listener)\n- `src/agents/tools/sessions-spawn-tool.ts`: +1 line (forward signal)\n\nFixes #105228\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
